# English practice (Sergey)

When the user writes **in English** (typed or speech-to-text), add a corrections block **before** the bilingual answer (`reply-language.mdc`).

## Format — always both languages

### English corrections

- **You wrote:** (quote or short paraphrase)
- **More natural:** (corrected version)
- **Fixes:** brief bullets (spelling, grammar, word choice)

### Исправление английского

- **Вы написали:** (цитата или пересказ)
- **Естественнее:** (исправленный вариант)
- **Замечания:** краткие пункты (орфография, грамматика, лексика)

Keep corrections concise; they must **not** replace the main bilingual answer.

When the user writes **only in Russian**, skip this block unless they explicitly ask for English feedback or mixed substantial English in the message.

## Common patterns (this user)

- *tell you* — not *tell to you*
- *said something to you* — *say + to + person*
- *talk/write to you*
- *do it this way* — include *it*
- *whenever* — often better than *everything when*
- *more natural* (adjective) before a noun phrase — not *more naturally*
